      "stride": "Repudiation",
      "title": "Commits made by a shared agent identity cannot be traced to a requester",
      "scenario": "All pushes come from one agent token, so the git history shows the bot, not which developer asked for the fix or which issue comment steered it. After a malicious or damaging change, responders cannot tell whether a developer requested it, an injected comment caused it, or the token itself was stolen, which stalls incident response and lets the attacker repeat the trick.",
